FYI: I solved the above error:

"This application has failed to start because Rlapack.dll was not  
found.  Re-installing the application may fix this problem"

by adding the following to my PATH environment variable:

C:\Program Files\R\R-2.5.1\bin

However I found this out after pulling down the latest RPy from SVN,  
building it, and discovering that the RPy import problem is still  
broken in the trunk code (forgive my ignorance if it's been fixed  
elsewhere in the tree and I just missed it)

